N times.\n`WeatherClient.get` now retries when the server returns 503. It makes up to 3 attempts in total, waiting 0.5s and then 1s between them. I tested it against a local server set up to return 503 a chosen number of times, and it behaved as intended:\n\n| Server behaviour | Result | Requests made |\n|---|---|---|\n| Succeeds straight away | JSON returned | 1 |\n| 503 twice, then succeeds | JSON returned | 3 |\n| 503 every time | `HTTPError 503` raised | 3 |\n| 500 once | `HTTPError 500` raised | 1 |\n\nThe change is in `weather.py`:\n- **What gets retried:** only 503 responses (`urllib.error.HTTPError` with code 503). Other HTTP errors, network errors and timeouts fail immediately, as before.\n- **After the last attempt:** the final 503 error is raised to the caller unchanged.\n- **New settings:** two optional arguments on the constructor, `max_attempts=3` and `backoff=0.5` (seconds). The wait doubles each time.\n\nThe test was a one-off script, so no test file was added to the repo.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 6, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 0, "requests_cache_write": 212749, "requests_cost_usd": 1.098741, "requests_count": 6, "requests_input_uncached": 14, "requests_output": 1747, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial2", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 62, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-20T03:38:11.375435+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 55.86, "t_checker_s": 2.379, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_